  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing a playful naming preference",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material (top_text and bottom_text) which expresses a humorous, self-deprecating or lighthearted stance on naming seagulls. The text 'fine, i'll keep calling them seagulls..' and '...but, beach chickens sounds better.' implies the user is adopting the perspective of someone making a casual, humorous linguistic choice, projecting their own playful attitude onto the meme's text. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the tone and content of the text invite the viewer to identify with the speaker's whimsical perspective.",
